From: kusti420 <virtuaalnepannkook@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: gadget: report missed isochronous transfers per request

The A73 USB backport (6f6ff833223a "drivers: usb: Backport changes from A73")
moved dwc3_gadget_ep_cleanup_completed_requests() in
dwc3_gadget_endpoint_transfer_in_progress() above the DEPEVT_STATUS_MISSED_ISOC
check. Requests are now given back before status is set to -EXDEV, so an
isochronous request whose interval had passed (its data was never sent)
completes with status 0. Only requests with no_interrupt get -EXDEV, from the
TRB status (0d1c407b1a74 "usb: dwc3: gadget: Return proper request status").

Function drivers therefore cannot see missed isochronous transfers at all. On
the UVC gadget this means that when the request ring runs dry in the middle of
a frame, every payload appended afterwards is silently dropped (the transfer
stays behind schedule) and the host receives a truncated frame that it cannot
tell from a good one.

Take the status of isochronous requests from their TRB, as is already done for
no_interrupt requests: TRBSTS_MISSED_ISOC gives -EXDEV, anything else keeps the
event status (0, or -ECONNRESET on a bus error). Unlike the upstream ordering
(-EXDEV for every request completed by an event that has MISSED_ISOC set), only
the request that was actually missed is flagged.

Used by MonsterROM target/a52sxq/patches/usb_webcam.
---
diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/gadget.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/gadget.c
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/gadget.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/gadget.c
@@ -3596,8 +3596,15 @@
 	 * For the requests that don't set interrupt on completion, the driver
 	 * needs to check and return the status of the completed TRBs associated
 	 * with the request. Use the status of the last TRB of the request.
+	 *
+	 * Isochronous requests are completed before the event's MISSED_ISOC
+	 * status is looked at (dwc3_gadget_endpoint_transfer_in_progress()),
+	 * so their status has to come from the TRB as well: a TRB whose
+	 * interval had already passed was never sent, and the function driver
+	 * must see -EXDEV for it rather than a successful transfer.
 	 */
-	if (req->request.no_interrupt) {
+	if (req->request.no_interrupt ||
+	    (dep->endpoint.desc && usb_endpoint_xfer_isoc(dep->endpoint.desc))) {
 		struct dwc3_trb *trb;
 
 		trb = dwc3_ep_prev_trb(dep, dep->trb_dequeue);
@@ -3612,7 +3619,8 @@
 			/* Control endpoint only */
 		case DWC3_TRBSTS_OK:
 		default:
-			request_status = 0;
+			/* keep a bus error reported by the event itself */
+			request_status = req->request.no_interrupt ? 0 : status;
 			break;
 		}
 	} else {
